{"timestamp": "2026-09-21T17:17:22.256721", "data": {"url": "https://www.weather-forecast.com/locations/Dresden/forecasts/latest", "title": "Dresden Weather Forecast", "content": "English Fran\u00e7ais Deutch Espa\u00f1ol Nederlands \u65e5\u672c\u8a9e \u4e2d\u6587 Dresden Weather Forecast Dresden Weather Forecast Dresden (Saxony, Germany) forecast issued: 1 pm Mon 21 Sep 2026 local time | Updates in: hr min s | (Update imminent) Issued: 1 pm Mon 21 Sep 2026 local time | Updates in: hr min s | (Update imminent) Germany Dresden Dresden Weather Forecast. Providing a local hourly Dresden weather forecast of rain, sun, wind, humidity and temperature. The Long-range 12 day forecast also includes detail for Dresden weather today. Live weather reports from Dresden weather stations and weather warnings that include risk of thunder, high UV index and forecast gales. See the links below the 12-day Dresden weather forecast table for other cities and towns nearby along with weather conditions for local outdoor activities. Dresden is 111 m above sea level and located at 51.05\u00b0 N 13.75\u00b0 E . Dresden has a population of 486854. Local time in Dresden is CEST. Read More Alright folks, let\u2019s take a look at what\u2019s shaping up for us over the next couple of weeks. The overall pattern starts off a bit unsettled with some rain showers and cloudier spells, but don\u2019t worry \u2014 it\u2019s going to turn beautifully settled and mainly clear as we head deeper into the period. Temperatures will climb nicely, especially by late next week and into early October, feeling more like a warm extension of summer at times. Starting right now, this Monday afternoon we\u2019ve got rain showers moving through with a northwest breeze around 25 km/h, and temperatures hovering near 16\u00b0. Those showers continue into tonight, with lows dipping to about 9\u00b0 under a west-northwest wind around 15 km/h. Tuesday morning still has some clouds around, but by the afternoon we clear out nicely, hitting a high near 18\u00b0 under mostly sunny skies. Tuesday night turns partly cloudy with a light west wind, and lows around 10\u00b0. Wednesday is a stunner \u2014 mostly clear all day, with highs reaching 18\u00b0 in the afternoon and a refreshing northwest breeze around 10 km/h. Wednesday night stays clear and cool, dropping to about 13\u00b0. Then on Thursday, we see another change: rain showers return in the morning and light rain develops into the afternoon, with a west wind picking up to 20 km/h. Highs will only reach about 15\u00b0, and it\u2019ll feel cooler with wind chills around 12\u00b0. Thursday night remains cloudy with lows near 12\u00b0. Friday starts with light rain in the morning, and more light rain through the afternoon, but at least the wind backs off a bit. Highs near 16\u00b0. Friday night, some clouds linger but it stays dry, with lows around 11\u00b0. Now, here comes the good stuff. From Saturday onward, high pressure builds in and we\u2019re looking at a long stretch of mainly clear skies and warming temperatures. Saturday is a beauty \u2014 clear and sunny, with a high of 21\u00b0, and light southeast winds. Saturday night clear and cool, down to about 12\u00b0. Sunday continues the trend: mostly clear, with a high of 22\u00b0 under a gentle south-southeast breeze. Sunday night stays clear, lows near 15\u00b0. Monday the 28th? Absolutely gorgeous. Morning clear, afternoon clear and warm \u2014 highs climbing to 24\u00b0 with a light southeast wind. Monday night clear, lows around 16\u00b0. Tuesday the 29th looks even warmer. Clear skies all day, and the afternoon high soars to 25\u00b0, making it one of the warmest days in the forecast. Tuesday night partly cloudy but still mild, with lows near 17\u00b0. Wednesday the 30th will be the hottest day of the entire outlook. Morning some clouds, but the afternoon turns clear and we\u2019ll hit a high of 26\u00b0 \u2014 that\u2019s the peak temperature for this whole period. However, by Wednesday night a cold front approaches, bringing light rain and a shift to northwest winds around 15 km/h, with lows dropping to 15\u00b0. Into the first week of October, confidence decreases a bit, but here\u2019s the general idea. Thursday the 1st starts with rain showers in the morning, then some clouds in the afternoon with highs near 18\u00b0. Thursday night clearing out, lows around 13\u00b0. Friday the 2nd looks good \u2014 morning clear, afternoon clear and warm, highs near 22\u00b0. Friday night partly cloudy, lows about 16\u00b0. Saturday the 3rd: some clouds in the morning, then clearing to a sunny afternoon with highs near 23\u00b0, and calm winds. Saturday night clear, lows around 16\u00b0. Sunday the 4th: another fine day, morning clear, afternoon clear, highs near 22\u00b0 and light northeast breeze. Sunday night clear, lows about 15\u00b0. Monday the 5th: morning some clouds, but afternoon clears up nicely with a high of 24\u00b0. Monday night clear, lows near 15\u00b0. Finally, Tuesday the 6th: morning some clouds, then clearing with a high near 19\u00b0 under a north-northwest breeze. Tuesday night clear and cool, with lows dipping to 12\u00b0. So, the extremes? The highest temperature will be 26\u00b0 on Wednesday the 30th of September, and the lowest will be 9\u00b0 on Monday night the 21st. No significant rainfall or snowfall totals are expected \u2014 just occasional light rain and showers early on. Enjoy the beautiful stretch ahead! Read more \u25bc Dresden Weather Today (1\u20134 days) Light rain (total 7mm), mostly falling on Thu morning. Very mild (max 18\u00b0C on Wed afternoon, min 9\u00b0C on Tue morning). Winds decreasing (fresh winds from the WNW on Mon afternoon, light winds from the WSW by Tue night). Dresden Weather (5-7 days) Light rain (total 2.5mm), mostly falling on Fri afternoon. Warm (max 21\u00b0C on Sat afternoon, min 11\u00b0C on Sat morning). Wind will be generally light. 10 Day Dresden Weather (8\u201310 days) Mostly dry. Warm (max 25\u00b0C on Tue afternoon, min 15\u00b0C on Sun night). Wind will be generally light. Dresden Weather Next Week (11-13 days) Light rain (total 8mm), mostly falling on Wed night. Warm (max 26\u00b0C on Wed afternoon, min 12\u00b0C on Fri morning). Wind will be generally light. Dresden Weather Next Week (14-17 days) Mostly dry. Warm (max 24\u00b0C on Mon afternoon, min 11\u00b0C on Wed morning). Wind will be generally light. Change units Mon 21 Tuesday 22 Wednesday 23 Thursday 24 Friday 25 Saturday 26 Sunday 27 Monday 28 Tuesday 29 Wednesday 30 Thursday 1 Friday 2 Saturday 3 Sunday 4 Monday 5 Tuesday 6 PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night AM PM Night km/h 25 NW 15 WNW 15 WNW 15 NW 5 W 10 WNW 10 WNW 10 SSW 20 W 20 W 15 WSW 15 W 15 WNW 5 SW 5 SE 10 S 10 SSE 15 SSE 10 SSE 10 SSE 5 SSE 10 SE 10 SSE 10 SSE 10 SSE 10 SSE 15 SSE 10 S 15 NW 10 NNW 5 NNE 5 ESE 10 ESE 5 E 5 SSW 5 WNW 10 NW 0 SSW 5 ENE 10 NE 5 SE 5 SSE 5 NW 5 WSW 10 NW 10 NNW 0 NNE See all maps mm 1.4 1.1 0.1 0.1 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 0.3 4 0.4 0.4 0.2 1.3 0.2 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 6 1.9 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 max \u00b0 C 16 13 12 18 14 14 18 15 13 15 12 13 16 14 17 21 16 19 22 18 21 24 19 22 25 20 23 26 23 15 18 16 17 22 18 20 23 20 19 22 18 20 24 20 15 19 16 min \u00b0 C 16 9 9 16 10 10 17 13 12 14 12 12 16 11 11 21 12 12 22 15 15 24 16 16 25 17 17 26 15 15 17 13 12 21 16 16 22 16 15 22 15 15 23 15 14 19 12 chill \u00b0 C 14 7 7 15 10 9 17 12 11 12 10 11 15 11 11 21 11 11 22 14 15 24 16 16 25 17 16 26 15 14 17 13 12 21 16 16 22 16 15 22 15 15 23 15 14 19 12 Humid % 64 90 75 41 60 59 40 60 87 82 88 88 73 78 54 36 66 44 40 62 46 38 56 43 37 52 35 33 90 79 60 84 69 53 75 60 54 78 59 42 65 57